menu "CPE AT Telemetry Configuration"

    config CPE_AT_ENABLE
        bool "Enable AT telemetry (and modem reset before deliberate restarts)"
        default y
        help
            Open a second CDC port on the modem AT interface (vendor specific
            or CDC-ACM) and poll AT+CSQ / AT+COPS? / AT+CEREG? / AT+CGATT? /
            AT+CGACT? / AT+QCSQ / AT+QTEMP together with ATI / AT+CGSN once.
            The values are shown on the Web status page. Telemetry uses only
            read-only commands, so the data connection is not disturbed.
            The single state-changing command is AT+CFUN=1,1: before every
            deliberate restart (Web reboot, factory reset, OTA, reset button,
            controlled reboot) the modem is asked to reset so it re-enumerates
            cleanly after the ESP boots. This is best effort and bounded; a
            missing AT port never delays the restart.
            QCSQ and QTEMP are Quectel extensions: other modems simply answer
            ERROR and the corresponding rows stay "unknown". Disable this when
            the modem does not expose a usable AT interface next to the ECM
            one.

    config CPE_AT_POLL_INTERVAL_S
        depends on CPE_AT_ENABLE
        int "AT telemetry poll interval (seconds)"
        default 5
        range 5 600
        help
            How often signal strength, carrier and registration state are
            refreshed. The modem identity (model, firmware, IMEI) is read once
            when the AT port is opened.

    config CPE_AT_MODEM_RESET_TIMEOUT_MS
        depends on CPE_AT_ENABLE
        int "Modem reset wait before restart (ms)"
        default 3000
        range 1000 10000
        help
            How long a deliberate restart waits for the AT task to finish
            AT+CFUN=1,1. The wait is bounded on purpose: a wedged AT port must
            never delay the restart. 3000 ms covers one 2 s AT command plus the
            task wake-up and schedule jitter. Raise it only if a slow modem
            regularly answers FWKCHANG/OK later than that.

endmenu
